They do not exist. All you get is the (estimated) mean and variance of
the normal distribution that corresponds to the y*

> (2) My project objective is to calculate the effect of M on Y.I want to

> calculate the probabilities of falling in a particular category of Y
> when M=1 and when M=0. However,

